        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Kapaga',
            subtitle: 'Crazy Eights',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Kapaga is a traditional Greenlandic card game belonging to the 'Crazy Eights' family. It is a fast-paced shedding game played with a standard 52-card deck. The game is known for its high interaction, specific localized penalty rules, and the central role of the '8' and 'Ace' as power cards. It is a staple social activity in Greenlandic homes and community centers.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Brought to Greenland by Danish settlers and Arctic explorers, the game was adapted from European Crazy Eights (Olsen or Mau-Mau) to fit local social dynamics. The name 'Kapaga' is a localized phonetic name for a similar regional variant.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
